Buy high; return the difference!
Nanjing Real Estate Market Reappears "Price Difference Compensation" - China News Service
ZAKER News (Reporter Ma Zu-bo): In its October 10th investigation with the Yandang Evening News, it has been discovered that an expired 'price protection agreement' is back to the local real estate market again in Nanjing City, and one property developer on the New District of Jiangbei declared price compensation as part of its sales strategy. It offered buyers the chance for exchange if they choose this house instead of other options before their delivery date, and would refund any differences in prices accordingly.
The "Guaranteed Value" conditions are numerous
This residential project located in Jiangbei New District is called Baoji Yanzhong Cuiyun Tai and Mr. Sun, who came to view it last weekend, told reporters that he had noticed an announcement while touring the site.
His pictures sent to the journalist show that the developer of this project promised that if buyers purchase their housing during the period from February 1st to February 28th, they can have the right to change and refund the difference in price after both parties sign the sale contract up until delivery of corresponding property. If other properties of the same floor type, unit, etc., within the building or community with an advantage over those sold at earlier times exist (up to the level where it's not the same floor type), the developer shall offer buyers exchange privilege for such properties and refund any additional prices incurred.
Mr. Sun said that the sales consultant explained that this was just an “insurance agreement” – to give buyers peace of mind when they sell and not worry about developers lowering their prices for promotional purposes. "Now I’m afraid that once we buy it, it will be lowered in price anyway; going to the sales office to protest won’t leave me time to do so, and if I don’t protest, it’s really nice."
There are still many homebuyers who believe that “price guarantee agreements,” while reassuring buyers with their assurances, come at a high price.
Ms Zheng, who is planning to buy an affordable property in Jiangbei, says that properties with price guarantees must be of the same model and have similar layouts within the same building as well as in the same unit, so there aren’t many comparable options for buyers anyway. Thus, the threshold remains high.
There are also buyers who believe that because of information asymmetry, salespeople may offer additional concessions without disclosing them to customers, making it difficult for buyers to seek redress.
Whether it will be possible to retain home buyers is uncertain.
The reporter learned through online real estate in Nanjing that the residential building sold off 252 units of two buildings last November with an average unit price per square meter of RMB 39,843 for fully furnished housing and ranging from 105 to 129 square meters in area.
But two and a half months later, online real estate shows that as of now, there are a total of 157 unsold units in this project; it is up to 62.3%. In terms of the unit category 8th Floor, totaling 128 units with unsold units reaching 113 units. On the 7th floor, also totaling 124 units, among them 44 units are still not sold. The total sales number of the project is just 33, which accounts for merely 13%.
Market observers say that “price guarantee agreements” were also on the market in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of the previous year, the cross-Shan-Hu residential complex, Xiangtang West Garden, in Huangshan Road, attracted buyers' attention with its "Guaranteed Price Plan," which stipulated that if there was an increase in project discounts within one year, the company would refund any shortfall to existing residents.
From April 2011, Nanjing had nine projects offering part of their units to offer “compensation for price differences.”
"The real estate market is cooling; now more than ever, it needs a ‘shot in the arm’.
Senior real estate developer Shen Mr., who is an expert in property development, said that “price protection agreements” are also one of the marketing methods used by developers.
He believes that now enterprises need more confidence than home buyers, and offering the ‘guaranteed price’ policy is actually giving them encouragement.
On whether home buyers can be retained, he stated that this depends on multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, with some observation pending at present.
China's rescue team continues to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and has rescued four trapped individuals so far - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua News Agency reported on February 11 that after being rescued in Turkey, an action team of the China Rescue Team was dispatched with three teams and 45 rescue personnel to free another person from trapped.
Two search and evaluation teams were dispatched to conduct an assessment of 15 buildings on Wudaobaizhou Street.
So far, four people trapped have been rescued and five others killed have been located; assessments of life signs and risks at 25 collapsed structures have been carried out.
The rescue team will adjust its rescue forces scientifically according to actual conditions in the disaster area and on-site situations, and continue to deepen the rescue efforts.
The rescue team obtained information on assistance requests through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, verified them through various means including online inquiries and on-site searches.
To introduce the current rescue environment and conditions of building collapses to China’s Hong Kong Rescue Team and jointly carry out search operations.
Currently coordinating with the Italian search and rescue team for regional coordination (SSC5), while sending three members to work at the 5th Regional Search and Rescue Coordination Center in charge of operations, they communicated with multiple teams from Italy, Britain, Serbia, Slovakia, Oman, etc., learned about the UN rescue organization's operation and the situation of rescue teams from various countries.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and personnel support, adhering to the principle of unified command and prioritizing safety, enhancing on-site safety control, strengthening work discipline requirements, and clearly defining safety precautions.
Implement a continuous rotating on-duty and watchkeeping system to enhance camp area security management.
The medical staff of the rescue team provide health check-ups to their members every day and strengthen the medical protection for key personnel. The entire rescue team is currently healthy and has been conducting camp area disinfection.
After establishing their own campsite, the logistics support team has set up 4 major categories of tents – command communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, living accommodation, and dog kennels – totaling 26 tents to ensure that more than 30 sets of on-site rescue equipment were available for use.
Kim Jong-nam and his daughter have close father-daughter interactions, but his wife is left out in the cold.
(Reuters) North Korea held its 75th anniversary military parade on August 8 evening, with Kim Yo Jong, daughter of leader Kim Jong Un, attending and standing alongside her father at the podium.
North Korea’s state media on Wednesday released footage of Kim Il-sung holding his daughter in his arms and looking at her affectionately several times as they talk to each other privately. She gently caressed her father’s cheek with both hands and even touched his chest. The scene was broadcast across the country.
But Mrs. Li Xuezhong can only retreat to the sidelines.
According to reports from Korea Central Daily News and others, Kim Jong-un, along with his wife Kim Song-rae, took part in an official portrait ceremony held on July 7 that featured them seated between their parents at what was reportedly their customary central position. They also appeared together on the stage during the grand military parade for National Day marking the 75th anniversary of the founding of North Korea's army that same day.
The "Korean Central Television" of North Korea released footage after the military parade showing more scenes of father and daughter love.
Kim Jong-nam frequently looked at his daughter from the podium and never lost their smiles; they also whispered to each other in hushed tones. Kim Chol-ae once cupped her father’s cheeks with both hands, while Kim Jong-nam reciprocated with a radiant smile.
Other state-run media images show Kim Jong Nam and Kim Il Sung touching their father’s face with their hands as he sits on an indoor couch; they also hold each other’s hands while walking, and touch their father’s chest with their hands when holding each other’s hands.
And First Lady Li Xuezhong was always trailing behind or sitting to one side, never closer than a few steps from her husband and daughter.
Korean media noted that Kim’s Love has been increasingly spotted in public appearances since her first public appearance with the Kwangmyongsong-1 rocket, which was launched on November 18 last year. So far, she has appeared at five different occasions.
The North Korean media has referred to Kim Jong-nam as "the dearest sons and daughters" or "honorable sons and daughters." It also aired footage of Kim Jong-nam watching the military parade from the stands, shouting incoherently over and over “I shall always uphold bloodline” throughout.
These signs raise suspicion that Kim Il-sung is already predestined to be Kim Jong-un’s heir, according to an analysis in The Washington Post, which sees it as an indication of how Kim is elevating his teenage daughter to a successor position. However, there are also those who believe such assessments are premature given North Korea’s current political circumstances, especially with regards to the fact that Kim has sons.
"Fund E Account" Arrives: CSRC Grants Authority to Collect and Query All Funds Under Investors' Names - Economic Observer
Economic Observer reporter Chen Shan How difficult is it to aggregate account information due to the proliferation of fund purchase channels?
Always forgetting "the little gold piggy bank"?
The problems of the Kievan people will soon be resolved.
On February 10th, the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) announced that “Fund E Account” APP had been uploaded to and in public trial operation on all mobile application stores.
It is introduced that “Fund E Account” provides a one-stop query service for individual investors to obtain information on fund accounts and shares, aiming to address industry service pain points such as small and medium-sized investors forgetting their accounts or querying them intricately.
According to Wind data, as of December 31, 2022, there were approximately 156 domestic fund management companies and about RMB 2.6 trillion in managed funds; there were also 167 fund registration institutions for open-end funds and 411 sales institutions for open-end funds.
Each share registration institution's account system is independent and lacks an industry-wide query channel.
Industry observers say that at the end of 2021, there were over 72 million fund investors in China, meaning that half of the country’s population had invested in funds.
Previously, investors had to query their purchase situation through different sales channels, but with the “Fund E Account,” they can view all channels where they have purchased funds, allowing them to track their investment status in one glance.
What is the "Fund E Account" APP?
According to relevant documents, "Fund E Account" APP is a mobile application developed by China Securities Depository & Clearing Co., Ltd. in accordance with approval from the CSRC for the public offering fund industry portal app, providing one-stop query services for investors on all market open-end fund product holdings.
Investors can conveniently and quickly obtain their holdings of all funds managed by different fund managers through the “Fund E Account”. This will significantly enhance query efficiency.
Specifically, investors can query information about their fund accounts through the “Fund E Account,” including account information for funds opened at all public mutual fund managers and trading accounts opened at public fund sales institutions, as well as holdings of products such as open-end securities investment funds and collective asset management plans that do not have an upper limit on the number of investors.
Bloomberg's head of fund evaluation at Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation Research Center, Liu Yikang, told Caixin that investors can obtain all their onshore open-end fund holdings through the "Fund E Account" App in one go and help them recover 'forgotten assets'. More importantly, it has enabled customers to aggregate comprehensive information about their investment situation across accounts, helping them better understand their own investment status more promptly, accurately, and comprehensively, thereby optimizing their fund portfolio configuration and planning their financial arrangements accordingly.
How to Register and Use?
Journalists have noted that the “Fund E Account” app has been made available on Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and Vivo app stores but is still in public beta testing phase; users need to fill an invitation code during registration, and investors can contact their respective fund managers for assistance.
A fund manager from Shanghai’s largest mutual fund provided an invitation code to an economic observer reporter and said that during the trial phase of the APP, China Securities Depository & Clearing would provide each fund management company with a certain number of invitation codes; investors could obtain them over the phone and we would provide them.
After the pilot runs, users will no longer need invitation codes to register.
Translation requested.
Journalists registered and completed queries on their “Fund E Accounts,” which they downloaded from the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) website, in accordance with the relevant files of instructions for account registration and use. The entire process took no more than minutes. It was primarily divided into four steps: user registration, identity verification, fund account linking, and subscription query to public funds.
After completing this step of real-name authentication, clicking on the “Asset Fund Binding” button allows journalists to see all their purchased fund products from various fund sales platforms listed in the binding options (which can be linked to an account). After successful binding, they will be able to intuitively view their total investment in funds and start using the query function.
It is noteworthy that “Fund E Account” only provides query services to investors and cannot be used for subscription or redemption transactions.
The data displayed in Fund E account is generally three trading days before the date of query (T day).
For example, on February 10th, when you open the "Fund E Account," the total assets, fund shares, and net asset value displayed under the Asset page correspond to the date three trading days prior to that, which is February 7th.
