Multilateral data declines indicate underperforming Taiwan economy in the new year - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua Taipei Feb 11 (Reporter Zhao Bo and Huang Yang): A year of five reds, a seven-month contraction in manufacturing Purchasing Manager’s Index (PMI), and a three-digit consumer prices index (CPI). In recent months, Taiwan authorities have released economic data for January 2023.
Experts believe that Taiwan’s economic performance in the new year has been disappointing and growth pressures are mounting.
According to an announcement from the Department of Finance Affairs of Taiwan, Taiwan’s exports amounted to $31.51 billion in January this year, down 21.2% year-over-year, marking their fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of 11 major export categories fell year-on-year last year.
Rubber and plastic products, as well as optical instruments, posted the biggest declines of all sectors, falling year over year at rates of 37.6 percent and 35.7 percent respectively.
Electronic components exports fell 20.1% year on year, marking the largest decline in over a decade.
Among these, semiconductor sales fell 18.3%, marking its worst decline in four years.
Zhang Mian, acting head of Statistics Department in this ministry said that this shows that the weakening effect of demand for consumer electronics has spread to the industry, and electronic products have entered correction period.
Statistics show that in January Taiwan’s exports and imports dropped by double digits, with a trade surplus of just 2.34 billion US dollars, down to the lowest level since three years ago.
The Taiwan authorities’ finance bureau believes that global terminal demand is declining, industrial adjustments in inventory will suppress manufacturers' purchasing intentions for materials, and export weakness may not improve temporarily. The Taiwanese first-quarter exports could be worse than expected this year.
According to the Taiwan's Institute of Economics and Business Research, January’s manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index (PMI), after seasonal adjustment, stood at 40.4%, which dropped another 3.3 percentage points from December last year, extending the contractionary trend for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring index system, the Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) is considered to be at 50% as the turning point between expansion and contraction; if the index exceeds 50%, it indicates an expansion of the economy's prosperity, while a value below 50% signifies contraction.
Of the five-item aggregate component indicators of Taiwan’s Purchasing Managers’ Index for January, new orders, production, and manpower hiring contracted, while supplier delivery time decreased and inventory tightened.
All six industries have returned to contraction, with their order of contraction speed being Power and Machinery Industry (35.1%), Electronic and Optical Industry (35.2%), Chemical and Biomedical Technology Industry (39.2%), Raw Materials Industry (42.4%), Transportation Industry (42.6%), and Food and Textile Industry (45.7%).
Inflation-wise, Taiwan’s Main Counting and Statistical Office reported that the year-over-year increase of the Consumer Price Index (CPI) in January this year was 3.04%, which again surpassed the 3% mark since July last year.
Among them, vegetable prices jumped 28.25%, reaching their highest level in 17 months.
Committee Chairman of the “Main Counting Bureau,” Cao Zhihong, candidly admitted that the price increase for vegetables was indeed higher than expected. Without considering the impact of the Spring Festival, CPI should have been around 2.71% in January and February this year, with inflationary pressure still present, and it is at an all-time high.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy this year, experts are pessimistic according to reporting from media outlets such as “United Daily News” and Yahoo Finance on the island.
Professor Wu Daren from National Central University’s Economics Department said that export contraction may cause problems for exporters in the manufacturing sector with cash flow issues and an increase in default risk.
At the same time, falling orders lead to manufacturers reducing labor costs and affecting the labor market and household economies, which in turn impacts consumer demand.
Mr. Chou Ta-sing of the Institute of Taiwan Economic Research believes that the inflation situation in Europe and America is not resolved this year, and demand continues to shrink. Consequently, he forecasts that Taiwanese export will continue to suffer from decline throughout the first half of the year.
Since Taiwan’s economy relies on exports for support, and export demand is weakening, its overall growth performance over the year will likely be weaker than last year.
Newly-appointed central committee members, alternate members, and main-level officials at provincial and ministerial levels complete the learning seminar on implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China - Rolling News - Hunan Daily - Huasheng Online
The newly elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members of the Central Committee as well as leading cadres at provincial and ministerial levels have completed their training on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editorial Board Member: Li Suxiang] Font Size: 【Large | Medium | Small】
Xinhua News Agency reported that the Central Committee’s new members and candidates for membership in the Politburo Standing Committee as well as provincial and ministerial-level leading cadres who have joined the Communist Party of China (CPC) at the 20th National Congress of the CPC were gathered to attend a seminar on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress. The seminar concluded today afternoon at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance), where General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, Zhang Jie, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a speech summarizing the seminar.
He said that he would thoroughly study and implement the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar training class, with greater determination to uphold the “two establishments” and resolutely achieve the “two upholds,” strengthen his abilities and work hard to advance all tasks related to China’s modernization in accordance with the requirements of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era, and create achievements worthy of historical, practical, and people's judgment in fully building a modern socialist country and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar period, all trainees studied the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping, and learned about the important speeches delivered at the opening ceremony of the seminar by General Secretary Xi Jinping on behalf of the Central Committee of the CPC. They linked practice to in-depth study and discussion on major theoretical and practical issues concerning China’s modernization, thereby deepening their understanding of some key theories and practices related to the path of national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization. This strengthened their confidence and determination in leading the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the leadership of the Central Committee of the CPC led by Xi Jinping, as well as their sense of responsibility and mission towards fulfilling responsibilities and performing duties effectively and achieving a good start during the New Era and the new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, representatives from Class 10 made speeches to report and exchange their learning experiences.
Chai Qi stated that comprehending and practicing the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era as proposed by Xi Jinping and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC) is both an urgent task for the current period and one of long-term strategic importance. He emphasized that it requires adhering to the principle of “comprehensively studying, grasping thoroughly, and implementing fully” in order to promote work on comprehension and practice continually towards deeper levels, practical implementation, and reaching heart level.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
To diligently master and apply Marxist theory as one’s forte, consciously arm oneself with the Party’s innovative theories to guide one’s thoughts, practice, and work, and strive to achieve deep study, meticulous understanding, and firm implementation in these areas; truly learn to acquire unwavering belief, absolute loyalty, and mission commitment.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
To enhance capabilities to drive high-quality development, serve people’s livelihoods, and manage risks, we should vigorously promote an atmosphere of seeking guidance through investigation and research, and resolutely prevent and correct formalism and bureaucracy.
Zhi Tai Feng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu JinGuo, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony and Chen Xi presided over it.
VNA Hanoi – VNA correspondent for Vietnam’s Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Phuc and his wife have successfully completed their official visit to Singapore and Brunei, achieving comprehensive, practical, and specific results.
Wenmingzhigong Chairman participated in 30 different events within three days of his visits to Singapore and Brunei.
The gains have injected new impetus to deepen and broaden the strategic partnership between the two countries and the comprehensive partnership in Vietnamese language.
During his visit to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh reiterated Vietnam’s foreign policy of independence, diversification, and dynamism, willing to be good friends and reliable partners for all nations as well as responsible members of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in each country’s interest to promote the welfare of its people and contribute to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
At each meeting and negotiation, Prime Minister Fang Mingzheng agreed with their respective leaders of Singapore and Brunei that enhancing political trust with Vietnam can be enhanced through high-level visits of delegations and effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore have signed an Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Image from VNA (Vietnam News Agency)
Vingroup President Nguyen Phu Trong stressed during meetings with business leaders, seminars or at economic forums that Vietnam is open to and ready to create favorable conditions for Singaporean and Bruneian companies to expand their investments in digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, innovation and creativity sectors in the country.
This visit will deepen Vietnam’s cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, among others; it also creates new frameworks for cooperation in emerging fields like digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, sustainable development, etc.
King Sultan Hasmânarul Bolkiah of Brunei and Premier Foon Ming Jit are prepared to enter the bilateral meeting discussion session.
Image sourced from VNA News Agency
During his visits to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh’s Prime Minister has made time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of Vietnamese expatriates living there.
At bilateral meetings with leaders, Pham Minh Chinh urged his governments to pay more attention and create favorable conditions for the fair treatment of local Vietnamese communities so that they can contribute meaningfully to their societies and nurture better relations between China and Vietnam.
This suggestion has been endorsed and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Vice President Fang Mingzheng also shared with the leaders of both countries his desire for an ASEAN Community that is united, peaceful, stable and prosperous; they agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN member states while enhancing their role as a regional and international leader in the complex and ever-changing geopolitical environment.
With its important achievements, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made an official visit to Singapore and Brunei to effectively implement the Party’s Third Congress’ priority of strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors through effective implementation of the 12th Conclusion (12-KL/TW) of the Central Committee Political Bureau on Vietnamese Foreign Affairs in the new situation, as well as making positive contributions to mobilizing the strength of the entire nation.
(Complete)
What was the "object" that was shot down over Al Ain?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
On Friday afternoon this week (Feb 10), the US military used its most advanced stealth fighter jet, the F-22, to shoot down an unidentified object that had been flying over Alaska in America.
The strike took place ten miles from Alaska's coast.
This is the second time in less than a week that US forces have downed an aerial target.
An espionage balloon from China was shot down over South Carolina near the coast of North Carolina after drifting in US airspace for several days last Saturday.
The Pentagon said that the second object downed was first detected in U.S. airspace on Thursday evening near the Alaska northeast corner and tracked by American military authorities as it moved at an altitude of about 12 kilometers (39,000 feet) above sea level, approximately one-quarter the size of the smaller Chinese spy balloon previously shot down.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no indication that this object could be controllable.
US National Security Council spokesman John Kobie Friday said that although the precise look of this object in the stratosphere is unclear, “it poses a reasonable threat to the safety of commercial air travel.”
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe says, "We call it an ‘object’ because that is currently our best description."
President Biden listened to Pentagon advice before ordering the destruction of the object and added that he made his decision “very carefully.”
The official description of this object in US terms can be summarized as follows: it is roughly the size of a small car, without a steering wheel or suspension system, and at an altitude of around 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have come from China, like that spy balloon intruding American airspace and the Chinese balloon floating above Latin America, performing some task at different locations.
And some have compared this object in Alaska to an “unidentified flying object,” or U.F.O.
The report from Newsweek magazine cites former US Congressman Peter Meijer, who tweeted on Friday, “I really hope this ‘unidentified flying object’ is an espionage balloon rather than a legitimate UFO.”
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Meeks tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
The Weekly News says that not just Megadeth is doubting if the object in question is an UFO.
Rep. Tim Burchett of Tennessee’s Republican Party criticized the government’s decision to cover up intelligence last month and called on the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (ODNI) to release reports about “unidentified flying objects.”
Iran Celebrates Revolution Anniversary; Hackers Support Protests with President's TV Address Hijacked
Iran’s Islamic Republic held an official rally to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution on Saturday and briefly interrupted President Ebrahim Raisi’s television address when a group of hackers attacked it.
The president’s televised address was interrupted for about a minute on the Internet, and a group of Iranian hackers known as “Edalat Ali (Ali Justice)” appeared on screen.
There was also some one shouting “Islamic Republic die.”
Reuters today reports that Iran is celebrating its revolution anniversary and hackers have disrupted national TV broadcasts.
The Iranian authorities marked the 44th anniversary of Iran’s Islamic Revolution yesterday with calls from hardliners in Shiraz for an end to their tenure as Tehran’s government is confronted with the most audacious challenge ever raised by young protesters demanding that they be replaced. But Shiraz still urges “the deceived youth” to repent so that they can receive pardons from Iran's supreme leaders.
After Mahsa Amini, 22, died in custody of Iran’s morality police on September 16, nationwide protests erupted across the country, still in Iran.
The Iranian security forces have ruthlessly suppressed protests, making this one of the most powerful challenges to Islamic Republic since the overthrow of the monarchy in 1979.
As part of an amnesty in celebration of the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities freed Friday two political prisoners who had been on hunger strike: Farkhaddin Mesbah-Yazdi and Fariba Adel-Haeri, an Iranian-French scholar.
Earlier Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty decree that included some of those arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to the report of Human Rights Advocacy and Action Network (HRANA), as of Friday, at least 528 protesters had been killed, including 71 minors.
The report says that another seventy government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that as many as 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for voting at Saturday’s demonstration to show opposition to protests and support of government.
On Friday evening of the 40th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, official media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, with people shouting “Allahu Akbar!”
(God is the greatest! )
However, there is also much shouting in assemblies of “Dictator must die!”
And videos posted on social media of “The Death of Islamic Republic”.
Saturday, the government TV broadcast live footage of official gatherings across all states.
In Tehran, as part of an official celebration, displays were held showcasing indigenous anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine frigates, and other military equipment.
Lestat’s speeches on the presidential campaign are invariably interrupted with chants of “get lost,” one that has become a hallmark at state conventions.
The crowd chanted "Israel must die."
Reuters reports that Adelkha, who has been in prison since 2019 and is one of seven French nationals held in Iran, is a factor in deteriorating relations between Paris and Tehran over recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison for national security offenses in 2020.
They later confined her at home but she returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denies these charges.
And just one week before Mesa Millar was released, supporters warned that he faced a death risk due to his fast-acting protests.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting mandatory headscarf wearing.
The French Ministry of Foreign Affairs responded on Friday to Adel Khah’s release and called for her freedom “including if she is willing, allowing her to return to France.”
